  "status": "Approved",
  "description": "Refurbishment and reconfiguration of existing school building to provide enhanced SEND facilities, including internal alterations, installation of new doors and windows, formation of external decking and canopy, and associated landscaping works to create a dedicated SEND garden, together with ancillary drainage and external works",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "Condition : 1 - The development hereby permitted must be begun not later than the end of three years from the date of this permission.\r\n\r\nReason: In order to comply with the provisions of Section 91 of the Town and Country Planning Act 1990 (as amended).\r\n\r\n",
    "Condition : 2 - The development hereby permitted shall be carried out in accordance with the following approved plans: 25003_PL-0001_REV03_Location Plan, 25003_PL-0002_REV01_Existing Site Plan, 25003_PL-0101_REV01_Existing Ground Floor Plan, 25003_PL-1102_REV01_Proposed Site Plan, 25003_PL-0102_REV01_Existing SEND AREA Plan, 25003_PL-1102_REV06_ Proposed SEND Area and Lanscaping Plan, 25003_PL-1201_REV02_ Existing Elevations 1, 25003_PL-1202_REV02_Exisiting Elevations 2, 25003_PL-1203_REV02_Existing Elevations 3, 25003_PL-1204_REV02_Proposed Elevations 1, 25003_PL-1205_REV02_Proposed Elevations 2, 25003_PL-1206_REV02_Proposed Elevations 3, 25003_PL-1301_REV01_ Existing Sections, 25003_PL-1302_REV01_ Proposed Sections, 25003_PL-1401_REV02_Demolition Plan, 25003_PL-8001_REV01_Existing Isometric, 25003_PL-8101_REV01_Proposed Isometric, Planning Statement Cover Letter dated March 2026, Design Heritage and Sustainability Statement, Ecology Note and Biodiversity Net Gain Assessment,  Arboricultural Report.\r\n\r\n\r\nReason: For the avoidance of doubt and in the interest of proper planning.\r\n",
    "Condition : 3 - All new external work shall be carried out in materials that resemble, as closely as possible, in colour and texture those of the existing building, unless otherwise specified in the approved application. \r\n\r\nReason: To safeguard the appearance of the premises and the character of the immediate area in accordance with the requirements of policies D1 and D2 of the London Borough of Camden Local Plan 2017. \r\n",
    "Condition : 4 - Before the relevant part of the work is begun, detailed drawings, or samples of materials as appropriate, in respect of the following, shall be submitted to and approved in writing by the local planning authority: \r\n\r\na) Details of the proposed glazed doors, the details of which should be matched to the design of the existing fenestration. Reason to harmonise the architectural detailing of the building.\r\n\r\nb) Details including materials of the proposed the proposed lean-to canopy and play area canopy. These features will be within the views from the public highway and therefore should be sympathetic to the setting of the school.\r\n\r\nc) Details of the boundary treatment(s) around the SEND play area. This area will be within the views from the public highway and therefore should be sympathetic to the setting of the school.\r\n\r\n\r\nReason:  To safeguard the appearance of the premises and the character of the immediate area in accordance with the requirements of policy D1 and D2 of the London Borough of Camden Local Plan 2017.\r\n",
    "Condition : 5 - Prior to the commencement of works on site, tree protection measures shall be installed and working practices adopted in accordance with the document entitled 'Arboricultural Report \" dated March 2026 by The Mayhew Consultancy Ltd.  All trees on the site, or parts of trees grow from adjoining sites, unless shown on the permitted drawings as being removed, shall be retained and protected from damage in accordance with BS5837:2012 and with the approved protection details. The development shall be monitored by the project arboriculturalist in accordance with the approved report.\r\n \r\nReason: To ensure that the development will not have an adverse effect on existing trees and in order to maintain the character and amenity of the area in accordance with the requirements of policies A2 and A3 of the Camden Local Plan.\r\n",
    "Condition : 6 - All hard and soft landscaping works shall be carried out in accordance with the approved landscape details [by not later than the end of the planting season following completion of the development or any phase of the development] [, prior to the occupation for the permitted use of the development or any phase of the development], whichever is the sooner. Any trees or areas of planting (including trees existing at the outset of the development other than those indicated to be removed) which, within a period of 5 years from the completion of the development, die, are removed or become seriously damaged or diseased, shall be replaced as soon as is reasonably possible and, in any case, by not later than the end of the following planting season, with others of similar size and species, unless the local planning authority gives written consent to any variation.\r\n\r\nReason: To ensure that the landscaping is carried out within a reasonable period and to maintain a high quality of visual amenity in the scheme in accordance with the requirements of policies A2, A3,  D1 and D2 of the London Borough of Camden Local Plan 2017.\r\n"
  ],
